  "body": "<p class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\" data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"116\">Coco Gauff joined select company with a 6-2, 6-4 victory against Jessica Pegula in the Cincinnati Open final Sunday.</p>\n<p data-start=\"118\" data-end=\"478\">By winning the tournament’s first all-American final since 1970, Gauff did more than capture her first title of the year on the WTA Tour Driven by Mercedes-Benz. She joined Serena Williams and Victoria Azarenka as the only women to win the WTA 1000 event twice. Gauff also won the title in 2023 before claiming her first Grand Slam championship at the US Open.</p>\n<p data-start=\"480\" data-end=\"656\">Gauff was dominant throughout the week. After dropping the opening set of her first match against Liudmila Samsonova, she won 12 consecutive sets while conceding just 32 games.</p>\n<p data-start=\"658\" data-end=\"865\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">Speaking to reporters after the final, Gauff stopped short of suggesting that her Cincinnati run would lead to another US Open title. But she said the confidence she gained should serve her well in New York.</p><div class=\"articleWidget center\">\n        <aside class=\"instagram-post embeddable-widget embeddable-widget--floating embeddable-widget--centered-mobile \"><blockquote class=\"instagram-media\" data-instgrm-captioned data-instgrm-permalink=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DcZ5_E1NpEz/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_campaign=loading\" data-instgrm-version=\"14\" style=\" background:#FFF; border:0; border-radius:3px; box-shadow:0 0 1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.5),0 1px 10px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.15); margin: 1px; max-width:540px; min-width:326px; padding:0; width:99.375%; width:-webkit-calc(100% - 2px); width:calc(100% - 2px);\"><div style=\"padding:16px;\"> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DcZ5_E1NpEz/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_campaign=loading\" style=\" background:#FFFFFF; line-height:0; padding:0 0; text-align:center; text-decoration:none; width:100%;\" targ